course: dictionary
lesson: 4661
title: Hobbies and lists
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hobby is something you enjoy doing in your free time, not as a job. «My hobby is drawing» tells the reader what you like doing when school and homework are finished. Drawing, football, collecting and gardening are all hobbies.
explain: You will often see hobbies in a list: «My hobbies are cooking, my dog, and reading.» The commas show where each item ends. Without them, «cooking my dog and reading» sounds terrible, so commas help the reader understand exactly what you mean.
explain: You can say you do something «as a hobby», or talk about your «hobbies and interests». If you want to try something new, you can «take up a hobby». Friends do not need the same hobbies to be close: «Best friends can like different things and do different hobbies and still be close.»
fact: A hobby is something you enjoy doing in your free time, not as a job.
fact: «Hobby» is a noun. Its plural is «hobbies», because y changes to ie.
fact: Useful phrases are «take up a hobby», «as a hobby», and «hobbies and interests».
fact: Commas separate the items in a list, so «cooking, my dog, and reading» is a clear list.
fact: Be careful about sharing your hobbies and school with people you do not know online, because a stranger can use that information to trick you.
exercise: What is a hobby? | *Something you enjoy doing in your free time | A rule that keeps you safe at school | A job you are paid to do
exercise: Which word is the plural of hobby? | *hobbies | hobbis | hobby's | hobbys
exercise: Which sentence makes a clear list? | *My hobbies are cooking, my dog, and reading. | My hobbies are, cooking my dog and reading. | My hobbies are cooking my dog and reading.
test: «Best friends can like different things and do different hobbies and still be close.» What does this sentence tell us? | You must have exactly the same hobbies as your best friend | Best friends never do hobbies | *You can have different hobbies from a friend and still be close
test: Which phrase means you have started a new hobby? | Give up a hobby | *Take up a hobby | Buy a hobby | Finish a hobby
exam: Which of these is NOT a hobby? | Drawing | Gardening | Football | *Working as a shop assistant for money
